    {"severity": "warning", "path": "src/bathos/compact.py", "line": 306, "issue": "_open_db structural check is gated by `db_path.exists() and db_path.stat().st_size > 0`. But `duckdb.connect(str(db_path))` on a non-existent path CREATES the file. So when _open_db is called on a fresh / empty target via verify_warm, the file will exist and the size will be > 0 (DuckDB writes a header immediately), and the check will proceed and fail on `_schema_meta` missing — which is the desired behavior for verify_warm (it requires a compacted DB). However, this is non-obvious; a reader will think the guard skips the check for empty files.", "fix": "Add a comment explaining the guard is defensive for the file-deleted-between-connect-and-check race, and that _schema_meta MUST exist after any successful compact()."},
